Complete a trace table for the following Python code. Show the values of i, count and the final output.
count = 0
for i in range(1, 6):
    if i % 2 == 0:
        count = count + 1
print(count)

Describe what the following code does. Write your answer as a plain-English description of the purpose of the program.
for i in range(1, 11):
    if i % 3 == 0:
        print(i)

Complete a trace table for the following Python code. Show the values of row, value and the output at each step.
grid = [[1, 2], [3, 4]]
for row in grid:
    for value in row:
        print(value)

Identify the error in the following code, and write a corrected version.
student = {"name": "Amir", "score": 78}
print(student.name)
